    "long_instructions": "You are a machine learning engineer designing a program that predicts how much a ticket to a particular theatre will cost. From the data, you’ve learned that theater ticket prices vary based on how far away they are from the stage. Tickets usually cost **$40.00** for the front row and prices go down by about **$0.50** for each foot back from the stage.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Complete the `predict_cost` function. It should use the y-intercept and slope you’ve learned to predict the cost of the ticket.\r\n2. Print a message to let the user know how far away they are from the stage and what their estimated ticket cost is.\r\n",
